@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-88-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-top-layer`
IMPORT `ito-125c-interest`

-- Tests for s 125C (interest received by an individual). Expected values were worked by hand from the section
-- ((b): top layer, rate at most 25%; (c)(1): 15%; (d): the rate of s 121; (e): outside) before they were run.
-- The scales are the ones s 121 prints (see tests-top-layer.l4). All amounts and holdings are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 125C`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN u IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a band ending at` u `at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS JUST u
        `rate of the band`        IS r

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a last band at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS NOTHING
        `rate of the band`        IS r

`the scale of s 121(a)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

`the scale of s 121(b)(1)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 84_120 `at the rate` (10%),
         `a band ending at` 120_720 `at the rate` (14%),
         `a band ending at` 228_000 `at the rate` (20%),
         `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
`a profits holding of` f MEANS
    `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` WITH
        `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS f
        `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS 0
        `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS 0

GIVETH A LIST OF `A person who may hold together with the person`
`no others` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The holdings of a person on one day`
`a profits record on` d `of` f MEANS
    `The holdings of a person on one day` WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `the person's own holdings that day` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS `no others`

GIVETH A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
`no records` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the readings with the cap read as` c MEANS
    `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` WITH
        `together with another`                   IS `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
        `counting the days of a period`           IS `declined where the way of counting changes the answer`
        `half the holding expenses`               IS `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`
        `the twelve months before a day`          IS `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`
        `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS c
        `where each part stands in the top layer` IS `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`
        `the real gain for the middle part` IS `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`
        `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

`the default readings` MEANS `the readings with the cap read as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`

-- An ordinary receipt: the amount, how it is linked, and no condition of (d) or (e).
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      link   IS A `How the property carrying the interest is linked to the index`
GIVETH AN `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C`
`an ordinary receipt of` amount `, linked as` link MEANS
    `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C` WITH
        `the interest` IS amount
        `how the property carrying the interest is linked` IS link
        `the interest is income under section 2(1), or is recorded or must be recorded in the individual's books` IS FALSE
        `the individual claimed a deduction of interest expenses and linkage differences on the property` IS FALSE
        `the individual's holdings in the paying body` IS `no records`
        `the individual is an employee of the paying body, supplies it services, sells it goods, or has other special relations with it` IS FALSE
        `the individual proved to the assessing officer that the rate of interest was fixed in good faith and not influenced by those relations` IS FALSE
        `paid from a study fund before the periods of section 9(16A) or (16B) passed, or from a provident fund for benefits to which section 3(d) applies` IS FALSE
        `another condition set by the Minister of Finance with the approval of the Finance Committee holds` IS FALSE
        `paid from a provident fund that is neither a fund for benefits nor a study fund, or from a fund for benefits taxed under section 87` IS FALSE
        `the interest is treated as interest income under section 3(h4)(3)` IS FALSE

GIVEN i IS AN `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C`
GIVETH AN `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C`
`the same with books kept` i MEANS
    `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C` WITH
        `the interest` IS i's `the interest`
        `how the property carrying the interest is linked` IS i's `how the property carrying the interest is linked`
        `the interest is income under section 2(1), or is recorded or must be recorded in the individual's books` IS TRUE
        `the individual claimed a deduction of interest expenses and linkage differences on the property` IS FALSE
        `the individual's holdings in the paying body` IS i's `the individual's holdings in the paying body`
        `the individual is an employee of the paying body, supplies it services, sells it goods, or has other special relations with it` IS FALSE
        `the individual proved to the assessing officer that the rate of interest was fixed in good faith and not influenced by those relations` IS FALSE
        `paid from a study fund before the periods of section 9(16A) or (16B) passed, or from a provident fund for benefits to which section 3(d) applies` IS FALSE
        `another condition set by the Minister of Finance with the approval of the Finance Committee holds` IS FALSE
        `paid from a provident fund that is neither a fund for benefits nor a study fund, or from a fund for benefits taxed under section 87` IS FALSE
        `the interest is treated as interest income under section 3(h4)(3)` IS FALSE

-- One flag raised at a time, by number of the paragraph of (d) it stands for.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
      recs IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
GIVETH AN `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C`
`a receipt of` amount `, fully linked, with books` b `deduction` c `special relations` d `proved good faith` e `study fund` f `Minister's condition` g `outside` h `deemed` i `holdings` recs MEANS
    `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C` WITH
        `the interest` IS amount
        `how the property carrying the interest is linked` IS `fully linked to the index`
        `the interest is income under section 2(1), or is recorded or must be recorded in the individual's books` IS b
        `the individual claimed a deduction of interest expenses and linkage differences on the property` IS c
        `the individual's holdings in the paying body` IS recs
        `the individual is an employee of the paying body, supplies it services, sells it goods, or has other special relations with it` IS d
        `the individual proved to the assessing officer that the rate of interest was fixed in good faith and not influenced by those relations` IS e
        `paid from a study fund before the periods of section 9(16A) or (16B) passed, or from a provident fund for benefits to which section 3(d) applies` IS f
        `another condition set by the Minister of Finance with the approval of the Finance Committee holds` IS g
        `paid from a provident fund that is neither a fund for benefits nor a study fund, or from a fund for benefits taxed under section 87` IS h
        `the interest is treated as interest income under section 3(h4)(3)` IS i

`the day of payment` MEANS YMD 2026 6 30

§§ `Paragraph (b): wholly index-linked interest, at most 25%, as the top layer`
-- 100,000 on other income 0 under scale (a): all in the 31% band, so 25% x 100,000 = 25,000.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `fully linked to the index`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 25_000
-- A reduced-rate individual with the interest wholly in the 10% band: 50,000 x 10% = 5,000.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 50_000 `, linked as` `fully linked to the index`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 5_000
-- Fork T1: other income 220,000, interest 100,000 under the (b)(1) scale: refused by default; 24,600 each band capped; 25,000 average capped.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `fully linked to the index`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the way a cap on the rate applies where the gain stands in several bands is not decided by the text, and here it changes the answer"
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `fully linked to the index`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` (`the readings with the cap read as` `the rate of each band is capped`) EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 24_600
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `fully linked to the index`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` (`the readings with the cap read as` `the average rate over the whole gain is capped`) EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 25_000

§§ `Paragraph (c)(1): interest not wholly linked to the index, 15%`
-- 100,000 x 15% = 15,000, for each of the three kinds, whatever the scale and the other income.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `not linked to the index`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 15_000
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `linked to the index in part of the rate of rise`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 15_000
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `not linked to the index until redemption or repayment`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 15_000

§§ `Paragraph (d): the rate of section 121 if one condition holds`
-- Each condition on its own, the interest otherwise wholly linked.
-- (d)(1) books.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` TRUE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
-- (d)(2) a deduction of interest expenses claimed.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` TRUE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
-- (d)(3) a material shareholder in the payer: 10% on the day; 9.99% is not.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of payment` `of` (10%))) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of payment` `of` (9.99%))) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 25_000
-- (d)(4) special relations, unless proved good faith: relations alone -> (d); relations and proof -> not (d) -> (b) 25,000; proof alone -> (b).
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` TRUE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` TRUE `proved good faith` TRUE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 25_000
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` TRUE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 25_000
-- (d)(5) a study fund paid early.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` TRUE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
-- (d)(6) a condition the Minister set.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` TRUE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
-- (d) overrides (c): not linked, books kept -> the rates of s 121, not 15%.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`the same with books kept` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `not linked to the index`)) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
-- Fork S4: a record of 10% on 30 June 2025 is inside the twelve months on one reading only; no other condition: refused. With books kept, (d) holds whatever the status: answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "whether the individual was a material shareholder depends on a reading section 88 leaves open, and here the treatment turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` TRUE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` FALSE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`

§§ `Paragraph (e): outside the section`
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` TRUE `deemed` FALSE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `outside section 125C`
-- Except interest treated as interest income under s 3(h4)(3): the section applies: (b) 25,000.
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`a receipt of` 100_000 `, fully linked, with books` FALSE `deduction` FALSE `special relations` FALSE `proved good faith` FALSE `study fund` FALSE `Minister's condition` FALSE `outside` TRUE `deemed` TRUE `holdings` `no records`) `received on` `the day of payment` `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 25_000

§§ `The date`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `not linked to the index`) `received on` (YMD 2011 12 31) `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the deposited text of section 125C is the text as amended in 2012, and the text before it is not deposited"
#ASSERT `s 125C — what is made of` (`an ordinary receipt of` 100_000 `, linked as` `not linked to the index`) `received on` (YMD 2012 1 1) `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS `taxed apart, the tax being` 15_000
